The muiTreeView R package is released under the MIT License
(see the LICENSE file).

The package bundles a pre-built JavaScript file
('inst/www/muiTreeView/x-tree-view.js') that includes minified
third-party code. License headers preserved by the bundler are in:

    inst/www/muiTreeView/x-tree-view.js.LICENSE.txt

Bundled third-party libraries
-----------------------------

  Library                  License  Copyright holder
  -----------------------  -------  -----------------------------------------
  @mui/x-tree-view         MIT      Copyright (c) MUI
  @mui/x-internals         MIT      Copyright (c) MUI
  @base-ui/utils           MIT      Copyright (c) MUI
  @mui/system (subpaths)   MIT      Copyright (c) MUI
  react-is, prop-types,
    use-sync-external-
    store                  MIT      Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc.
                                    and affiliates
  react-transition-group   BSD-3    Copyright (c) 2018, React Community
  @babel/runtime           MIT      Copyright (c) 2014-present Sebastian
                                    McKenzie and other contributors
  clsx                     MIT      Copyright (c) Luke Edwards
  reselect                 MIT      Copyright (c) 2015-2018 Reselect
                                    Contributors

The 'react', 'react-dom', '@mui/material', '@mui/utils',
'@mui/private-theming', '@mui/styled-engine', '@emotion/react',
'@emotion/styled' and '@emotion/cache' libraries are declared as
external dependencies of the bundled JavaScript and are provided at
runtime by 'shiny.react' and 'muiMaterial'; they are not themselves
redistributed inside this package. Deep subpath imports of
'@mui/system' (e.g. ThemeProvider, createStyled) are bundled as
transitive dependencies of '@mui/x-tree-view'.

